I am developing clickstream user tracking for one of my apps and writing the final data with onSessionEnded...but it seems like only session values are accessible inside of onSessionEnded...how can I access all the variables from within onSessionEnded?

Here is the tracking code:
observeEvent(session$onSessionEnded,{
    userTracking$endTime<-Sys.time()
    userTracking$totalTime<-as.numeric(difftime(userTracking$endTime,userTracking$startTime,units="mins"))
    userTracking$user<-ifelse(is.null(session$user),"unauthenticated",session$user)
    userTracking$Restricted<-as.logical(sum(grep('shiny_ru',groups())))
    userTracking$homeSearch<-userTime$homeSearch
    userTracking$homeTrends<-userTime$homeTrends
    userTracking$topicModeling<-userTime$topicModeling
    userTracking$trends<-userTime$trends
    userTracking$about<-userTime$about
    write.table(userTracking, file = "userTracking.txt",append = FALSE, row.names = FALSE, col.names = TRUE, sep = "|")
  })
all the "userTime$" reactiveValues are zero when the table is written even though the app code updates them every second.

How can I pass these time values to onSessionEnded so they can be logged appropriately?

